PopSNES - License
=================

PopSNES is an unofficial, non-commercial port of the snes9x2002
libretro core to the SHARP Brain PW-G5300 (Windows CE, ARM). Its license
has two levels.

1. PopSNES as a whole: the Snes9x license (non-commercial only)
----------------------------------------------------------------------

PopSNES as a whole (AppMain.exe, and the source published in this
repository) is distributed on the same terms as upstream snes9x2002:
the original Snes9x license, reproduced in full in section 3 below (and
in LICENSES/LicenseRef-Snes9x.txt). It is a NON-COMMERCIAL /
personal-use license: PopSNES may not be sold, bundled with anything
sold, or distributed only to people who paid. It is not an OSI/FSF-free
license.

The upstream files are not all under this one license: the DSP-1 code
in src/dsp1emu.c (by the ZSNES Team, compiled in through src/dsp1.c)
is under the GNU GPL, version 2 or later, and some upstream files
carry no license notice at all. This file does not state a single
license for the whole beyond "the same terms as upstream"; see
CE/THIRDPARTY_LICENSES.txt for each part.

2. PopSNES's own code: MIT
----------------------------------------------------------------------

This MIT license covers only PopSNES's own code listed in CE/LICENSING.md
(the files marked "SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT": the CE/ frontend
except the font data, the mascot images and the icon). PopSNES as a
whole is distributed on the same terms as upstream (section 1):
non-commercial only.

